ity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"73"},"sourceKey":"value","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"66"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"7ebed3d5-41a9-44cd-8e64-b7273d291b6c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"34"},"sourceKey":"value","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"44"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"d9b67404-267d-4702-964b-695c45301acc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"position":{"xMin":-928.9998,"yMin":-930.9999,"xMax":795.0007,"yMax":-161.9998},"label":"Gravity","comment":"Get
      the inbuilt gravity in Unity (Y axis which is up/down) and multiply it by a
      number so we have  little more control over it. Feel free to experiment with
      the exposd variables for deeper understanding.","color":{"r":0.0,"g":0.0,"b":0.0,"a":1.0},"guid":"e9f682cd-b50b-4336-b35f-85a55996db36","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-1988.0,"yMin":-521.0,"xMax":-1195.0,"yMax":-124.0},"label":"Freeze
      Player when Talking","comment":"This grabs the object type scene variable I
      made ''dialoguesystemcontainer'' and basically says, is the object active or
      not? Essentially is it true/false. If false, I can move, if true you will see
      there is no link to movement nodes... so no movement.","color":{"r":1.0,"g":0.5,"b":1.0,"a":1.0},"guid":"a1c5d9f8-1897-4233-a92c-33c82553bb00","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-1116.333,"yMin":-93.11111,"xMax":-872.9999,"yMax":147.4445},"label":"Grounded","comment":"A
      common term in game development. So common that Unity added a unique node to
      its ''CharacterController''. We have made our charcater  an object variable
      and dragged our character controller component from our playercontroller into
      the slot. We named the variable ''CharCon'' and have connected it in so we
      can find if ''CharCon'' is grounded. \n\nLook at the object variables on this
      graph to see :)","color":{"r":0.5321615,"g":0.6320754,"b":0.5277234,"a":1.0},"guid":"f28f2e6d-348a-442e-963a-03f103d94ba5","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":888.0,"yMin":229.0,"xMax":1178.0,"yMax":484.0},"label":"Move","comment":"Another
      unique node Unity has added in like the ''Grounded'' node. Unity lets us input
      some vector math and allows us to move a the character controller. We need
      to have a character controller to use with these nodes so we have our ''CharCon''
      added. ","color":{"r":0.5321615,"g":0.6320754,"b":0.5277234,"a":1.0},"guid":"01131552-9722-41e7-ac13-1bcf58abc18a","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-2039.0,"yMin":77.0,"xMax":-1687.0,"yMax":326.0},"label":"Input","comment":"I
      did demo this in lesson but we basically created our own ''Player Inputs''
      and added some actions. Please look in the project folder in the ''Player''
      folder for ''PlayerController''. Double click to open and you will see ''Move''
      in there as well as another one created called ''Interact''.\n\nNow there are
      built in input/action but I like to add my own as it keeps things simple.","color":{"r":0.5,"g":0.8868377,"b":1.0,"a":1.0},"guid":"d59f408e-8a77-4838-bfec-9b97a3d13285","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"}],"$version":"A"}}'
    _objectReferences: []
